+{%- comment -%}
+  Performance (2026-10-13): self-hosted copy of the two Google Fonts families that the Fontify app embed loaded from
+  fonts.googleapis.com as render-blocking stylesheets (Bebas Neue for headings, Poppins for p, a and li). Same files,
+  same unicode ranges and the same rules as the app, so the text renders identically, but without two extra
+  third-party connections and a blocking request. The Fontify embed is switched off in this theme (config/settings_data.json);
+  if the fonts are changed later in Fontify, re-enable the embed and remove this snippet from layout/theme.liquid.
+  Only the latin and latin-ext subsets are kept (Romanian needs both); the browser downloads a file only when the page uses it.
+  The files are Google's hinted build (the one Google sends to Windows and Linux). Its glyph outlines and metrics are identical
+  to the unhinted build Google sends to Android, macOS and iOS, which ignore hinting, so every platform renders as before.
